<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Llanbadarn Fawr</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Llanbadarn Fawr is a village near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aberystwyth">Aberystwyth</a> in Ceredigion, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, the site of an early medieval monastery associated with St Padarn. It was one of the leading church centres of Wales and the seat of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, and a centre of learning in the 11th century under the scholar Sulien and his sons. Its large 13th-century church still stands.</p></div>
